    "result": "The bug was in `sqlparse/tokens.py`: `_TokenType.__getattr__` had a comment claiming it skips dunder attribute access, but no actual guard existed, so any dunder lookup (e.g. `__deepcopy__` during `copy.deepcopy`) created a bogus `_TokenType` instance instead of raising `AttributeError`, leading to `TypeError: '_TokenType' object is not callable`. Added the missing dunder check to raise `AttributeError` as intended, restoring correct `copy`/`deepcopy` behavior."
  },
